# JobHunter / ZoNuLy — local secrets.
#
#   cp .env.example .env      (.env is gitignored — never commit it)
#
# Values here are read from the environment only. They are never written to
# config.yaml, never logged, and never passed on a command line — a secret reaches
# a child process through the environment, where `ps` and Task Manager cannot see
# it. `jobhunter.secret()` is the one way a credential enters this program.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- REQUIRED

# OpenRouter — the only paid model provider. Every LLM call in the pipeline goes
# through it, behind the aliases and budget caps in config.yaml.
#   https://openrouter.ai/keys
# Check it with: python scripts/run.py models check --live
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- OPTIONAL

# Exa semantic search, direct HTTP fallback for when mcporter is unavailable.
# Free tier: 1000 searches/month — https://exa.ai
# EXA_API_KEY=

# GitHub API. Only needed for the `github-api` fallback; the `gh` CLI uses its own
# login. Lifts the anonymous limit from 60/hr to 5000/hr.
# https://github.com/settings/tokens (scope: public_repo, or none for public data)
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ------------------------------------------------------ DEPLOYMENT (Railway et al.)
#
# None of these are needed to run locally. They exist so the same image can be put on
# a public URL without handing the internet a mailbox and a spending account.
# See `system docs/DEPLOY.md`.

# Turn the instance into a read-only exhibit: every write is refused, private
# endpoints are closed, and lead email addresses are masked. Set this on the public
# deployment and nowhere else.
# ZONULY_PUBLIC=1

# Lifts all of the above for whoever sends it as an `X-API-Key` header, so you can
# still drive your own instance from anywhere. Generate one with:
#   python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
# ZONULY_API_KEY=…

# Where the SQLite file lives. Absolute, or relative to the repo root. The image
# already sets this to the baked read-only snapshot; override it to point at a
# mounted volume if the deployment needs to write.
# ZONULY_DB_PATH=/app/demo.db

# Comma-separated browser origins allowed to call the API. Replaces the list in
# config.yaml when set — the Vercel URL is not knowable until the frontend exists.
# ZONULY_CORS_ORIGINS=https://zonuly.vercel.app

# Interface to bind. Containers need 0.0.0.0; the default 127.0.0.1 is deliberate
# locally. The port comes from $PORT, which the platform assigns.
# ZONULY_HOST=0.0.0.0
